  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find the measure of the side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ of the triangle $△ABC$ if $AC=3.1$, $BC=0.7,$ and the measure of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the measure of $\\overset{―}{AB}.$\n\nAccording to the triangle inequality theorem, the length of any side must be\n\n- greater than the difference between the lengths of the other two sides, and\n\n- less than the sum of those lengths.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Difference} & <x<\\text{Sum} \\\\ 3.1-0.7 & <x<3.1+0.7 \\\\ 2.4 & <x<3.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only integer satisfying this condition is $3.$",
